---
// Story 1-6. The Book page.
//
// ⚠️ THIS IS THE ONE PAGE THAT GETS THE FULL CLINIKO EMBED (D5). Every other
// page deep-links a single appointment type through <BookCta>. Two embeds on one
// page is a known defect class — Cliniko's own snippet hard-codes a single
// element id — and although ClinikoBooking fixes that properly with a per-
// instance id, one embed per page remains the design preference because deep
// links are lighter everywhere else.
//
// ⚠️ SCOPING IS CORRECTNESS, NOT POLISH. The Cliniko account is the SHARED
// Restore Health Clinic account: unscoped it offers 13 appointment types across
// 4 practitioners. An unscoped embed on Keegan's own site would let a visitor
// book Adrian Tomiak, Jake Williams or a naturopath. ClinikoBooking makes the
// business and practitioner ids a floor the caller cannot omit, so an unscoped
// URL is not constructible through this API.
//
// ⚠️ THE OLD PAGE'S BOOKING NOTE IS DELIBERATELY NOT PORTED. It read
// "Chiropractic and Mobility Services are provided within the same booking type.
// Just leave a message in the booking note indicating which you would like to
// focus on this session." That describes the PRE-redesign structure and is now
// false: the Movement Plan Analysis is its own bookable type (D1/D5). Porting it
// would have told patients to do the wrong thing. Recorded here because it is a
// deliberate removal, not an oversight.
//
// ⚠️ THE PHONE NUMBER ON THE OLD PAGE IS NOT OURS. It read "call the clinic on
// 0451 782 249" — that is Restore Health Clinic's line, not the NAP number. It
// must never reach schema or the footer (business.json phoneNote). This page
// uses business.phone, which is the number on the Google profile.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ClinikoBooking from '../components/ClinikoBooking.astro';
import business from '../data/business.json' with { type: 'json' };
// Story 1-16 hero ground. A treatment photograph rather than a room shot:
// the page is the booking page, so the ground should be the thing being booked.
import heroTreatment from '../assets/site/prone-tx.jpg';
// B3 — a STILL map, not a live embed. Keegan scrapped the Google Maps widget
// once it was priced: an iframe would have added an overseas data recipient to
// the privacy policy, set cookies against the deliberately cookieless analytics
// choice (D6), and reintroduced the consent-banner question the site does not
// need. This is a self-hosted PNG composited once from OpenStreetMap tiles —
// no API key, no cookies, and no third-party request when the page loads.
import clinicMap from '../assets/site/clinic-location-map.png';
// ART DIRECTION, and it is not decoration — see the zoom note beside the figure.
// The wide crop's labels are unreadable squeezed into a 327px phone column, and
// "you can see North Narrabeen and Freshwater" is Keegan's acceptance test, not
// a preference. Both crops are the SAME zoom and the same 14.3km north-to-south
// span; the narrow one just spends its pixels on height instead of width, which
// roughly doubles the rendered label size on a phone. He uses a Samsung, so the
// phone case is the one he will actually check.
import clinicMapNarrow from '../assets/site/clinic-location-map-narrow.png';
import { getImage } from 'astro:assets';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

const LAST_CHANGED = new Date('2026-07-31T00:00:00+10:00');
const { address } = business;

// <Image> cannot art-direct between two DIFFERENT source images, so the two
// crops are processed here and handed to a plain <picture>.
const mapWide = await getImage({ src: clinicMap, widths: [704, 1200], format: 'webp' });
const mapNarrow = await getImage({ src: clinicMapNarrow, widths: [420, 620], format: 'webp' });
const MAP_ALT =
  'Map of the Northern Beaches showing the clinic at Wheeler Heights, between Collaroy and Cromer, with North Narrabeen to the north and Freshwater to the south';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Book an Appointment | ${business.name}`}
  description="Book a chiropractic, movement or group class session with Keegan Baldwin at Restore Health Clinic, Wheeler Heights. Questions before booking? Call or email first."
  updated={LAST_CHANGED}
>
  {/* Story 1-16. The inner-page hero. The photograph is blurred and dimmed
      into a ground rather than shown as a picture, which is what makes the
      orange headline legible over it — see the measured note on .hero in
      BaseLayout. Decorative in that state, hence empty alt + aria-hidden. */}
  {/* Keegan 2026-08-06, "could be zoomed out". Same fix and same limit as the
      treatment hero: the strip was a shirt and a doorframe, with his face and
      the anatomy poster just above it. See --ml-hero-focus in BaseLayout. */}
  <section class="hero hero--page" style="--ml-hero-focus: 30%">
    <Image
      src={heroTreatment}
      alt=""
      aria-hidden="true"
      widths={[768, 1280, 1920]}
      sizes="100vw"
      loading="eager"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <h1>Book an appointment</h1>
      <p class="lead">
    Pick a time below. Every appointment type here is one of mine, so whichever you choose
    you are booking with me.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* Story 1-16 inner-page rhythm. A tinted band under the hero, as the target
      does — but a SHORT one, and the booking widget stays on the plain ground
      immediately below it. LN-4 is the reason: the embed is a reserved-height
      iframe whose content is tallest at the narrowest viewport, and 451px of it
      was once cut off on mobile. It does not go inside a decorative container
      that could constrain it again. */}
  <section class="section section--sage">
    <div class="intro">
      <p class="kicker">Wheeler Heights, Northern Beaches</p>
      <h2>Booking takes about a minute</h2>
      <p>
        Pick a type and a time below. If you have not seen me before, the one-hour new patient
        appointment is the one you want, whatever the reason for coming in. One thing to know before
        you pick: group classes run at Just Train Gym in Cromer, not at the clinic.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* One embed, scoped by construction. slugs omitted = all five of Keegan's
      types and nobody else's. */}
  <ClinikoBooking title="Book an appointment with Keegan" />

  <h2>Which appointment should I book?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>New patient, 1 hour, $120</strong>: if you have not seen me before, whatever the
      reason.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Existing patient, 30 minutes, $95</strong>: a return visit for a new or old problem.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Movement Plan Analysis, 1 hour, $160</strong>: the full mobility assessment that
      produces your personalised routine. You do not need to be in pain for this one.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Group classes, $20</strong>: mobility and flexibility, or handstands, at Just Train
      Gym in Cromer. <a href="/services/group-classes/">More about the classes</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Have questions before booking?</h2>
  <p>
    Get in touch and I will answer them first. Email{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> or call{' '}
    <a href={`tel:${business.phoneE164}`}>{business.phone}</a>.
  </p>

  {/* LN-6 / 1-15 section rhythm. The page's one band, on the where — the single
      fact a patient re-opens this page to check, and the one that has to survive
      being read at a traffic light. The Restore Health paragraph stays inside it
      because "the address is a clinic that is not mine" is the same answer. */}
  <section class="band">
  <h2>Where are the appointments?</h2>
  <p>
    All one-on-one in-person services are at {address.venue}, {address.streetAddress},{' '}
    {address.addressLocality} {address.addressRegion} {address.postalCode}. Group classes are held
    separately at Just Train Gym in Cromer.
  </p>
  {/* ⚠️ THE ZOOM IS THE ACCEPTANCE TEST, NOT A PREFERENCE. Keegan, 2026-08-07:
      "make sure the image chosen is zoomed out enough that it gives context.
      the dafualt zoom on my current site is far enoughout that you can see
      north narrabean and fresh water." So this is built at OSM zoom 13 over
      1200x900, which spans 14.3km north to south — North Narrabeen (~3km N)
      and Freshwater (~6km S) are both inside the frame AND their labels are
      still legible. Zooming in loses them; zooming out to 12 keeps them but
      shrinks every label. Verified by reading the rendered image.
      Re-cropping or re-centring this asset means re-checking those two names.

      The pin is a CSS overlay at dead centre rather than burnt into the raster,
      because the image is composited centred on the coordinates — so the marker
      cannot drift out of agreement with the map the way a drawn-on pin could. */}
  <figure class="map">
    <div class="map-frame">
      <picture>
        <source
          media="(max-width: 40rem)"
          srcset={mapNarrow.srcSet.attribute}
          sizes="100vw"
          width={620}
          height={900}
        />
        <img
          src={mapWide.src}
          srcset={mapWide.srcSet.attribute}
          sizes="(max-width: 44rem) 100vw, 44rem"
          width={1200}
          height={900}
          alt={MAP_ALT}
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </picture>
      <span class="map-pin" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>
    <figcaption>
      {address.venue}, {address.streetAddress}. Map data &copy;{' '}
      <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright" rel="noopener">OpenStreetMap contributors</a>.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
  {/* SM-9. The URL was the blank I refused to guess, because a fabricated
      domain sends real patients somewhere nobody checked. Keegan supplied it
      2026-07-31 and I confirmed it before publishing: 200, and the page is
      titled "Chiropractor Collaroy | Restore Health Clinic" and names both
      Keegan and the Lantana Avenue address. Verified, not assumed. */}
  <p>
    Restore Health Clinic is a separate business with its own practitioners and its own privacy
    arrangements. Your clinical records are held there, in their practice management system, not by
    this website.{' '}
    <a href="https://restorehealthclinic.com.au/" rel="noopener">Visit Restore Health Clinic</a>.
  </p>
  </section>

  <h2>Will I get a confirmation?</h2>
  <p>
    Yes, always. You will receive a confirmation email after booking. If you don’t see one, please
    check your spam folder, then get in touch if it still hasn’t arrived.
  </p>

  <h2>Can I claim my health fund?</h2>
  <p>
    Yes, if your private health fund includes chiropractic cover. We can process it in clinic at the
    time of payment if you have your card with you, or I can send you an invoice afterwards and you
    can claim it yourself.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }
  .map {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
  }
  /* The frame is what the pin is positioned against, so it has to wrap the
     image tightly — `display: block` on the img kills the inline-descender gap
     that would otherwise offset the pin by a few pixels. */
  .map-frame {
    position: relative;
    border-radius: 14px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .map-frame :global(img) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  /* Dead centre = the clinic, because the raster was composited around those
     coordinates. Orange is the accent's proper job here: a marker is a graphic,
     never text. The paper ring keeps it visible over both the green parkland
     and the grey street fill underneath. */
  .map-pin {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
    margin: -9px 0 0 -9px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--ml-accent);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--ml-paper), 0 1px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
  }
  figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--ml-muted);
  }
</style>
